    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "description",
      "value": "[auto-routed: 代码实验走真实执行] Execute the rigidity experiment pipeline to test the Manifold Intrinsicality Hypothesis (Hypothesis B). The workflow will: (1) generate constraint samples on a 2D manifold embedded in 10D space, (2) train single-hidden-layer ReLU networks of varying widths to fit the constraints, (3) determine the minimum width N_c(w) required to achieve validation error ≤ 1e-3 for each constraint count w, and (4) analyze the scaling of N_c(w) vs. log w to verify the logarithmic prediction. The experiment will compare against the Algebraic Variety (constant) and Landscape Complexity (linear) hypotheses."
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "skill",
      "value": "rigidity_experiment"
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "expected_prediction",
      "value": "The plot of N_c(w) vs. log w will show approximately linear growth with a slope proportional to the intrinsic dimension k=2, confirming the logarithmic scaling prediction N_c(w) ∝ k · log w. The R² of the linear fit will exceed 0.95, and the measured N_c(w) will be significantly below the linear prediction α·w and above the constant prediction N₀ for large w."
    },
